>ποδαπὸς τὸ γένος εἶ</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">;</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Ar.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Pax</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">186</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Pl.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Sph.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">216a</span> </span>: so in dat., <span class=\"gk\">γένει πολῖται</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">23.24</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">γένει υἱός</span>, opp. an adopted son, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">44.2</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οἱ ἐν γένει,</span> = συγγενεῖς, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1430</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οἱ ἔξω γένους</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Ant.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">660</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">οὐδὲν ἐν γένει</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Id.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1016</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">γένει προσήκειν τινί</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">An.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.6.1</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">γένει ἀπωτέρω εἶναι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">D.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">44.13</span> </span>: in gen., <span class=\"gk\">γένους εἶναί τινος</span> to be of his <b class=\"lex-tr\">race</b>, <span class=\"gk\">ἄναγνος καὶ γένους τοῦ Λαΐου</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">OT</cite> <span 